        {
          "id": 2749585278,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Wiretap modules and dissectors are, indeed, *not* part of the same library, they're in two separate ones.\n\nBoth of those libraries are *themselves* linked to the wsutil library, but I don't think BLF support is generic enough to go into wsutil.\n\nSo the alternatives are 1) separate static copies or 2) make the dissection library (the wireshark library) depend on the wiretap library.\n\nIn principle, perhaps they should be independent libraries, but, currently, they aren't completely independent in practice.  For example, the link-layer dissectors depend on `WTAP_ENCAP_` names from the wiretap library, so they depend on the way the wiretap library works.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
